body:
Jira Link: [DB-18526](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-18526)
### Description

Repro:

we specifically want to fail the CREATE DATABASE yugabyte command when we are executing it during pg_restore (but not the first time during initdb) and in such a way that some specific cleanup in ProcessPendingNamespace is executed. So the bug can be reproduced with the following diff:
```
--- a/src/yb/master/catalog_manager.cc
+++ b/src/yb/master/catalog_manager.cc
@@ -610,6 +610,8 @@ DECLARE_bool(enable_truncate_cdcsdk_table);
 DECLARE_bool(ysql_yb_enable_replica_identity);
 DECLARE_bool(ysql_yb_enable_implicit_dynamic_tables_logical_replication);

+std::atomic<int32_t> yugabyte_count{0};
+
 namespace yb::master {

 using std::shared_ptr;
@@ -3719,6 +3721,14 @@ Status CatalogManager::CopyPgsqlSysTables(const NamespaceInfo& ns,
   if (tables.empty()) {
     return Status::OK();
   }
+  if (ns.name() == "yugabyte") {
+    int32_t attempt = ++yugabyte_count;
+    LOG(INFO) << "yugabyte creation attempt #" << attempt;
+    
+    if (attempt == 2) {
+      return STATUS(InternalError, "inject CopyPgsqlSysTables failure for yugabyte");
+    }
+  }
   const uint32_t database_oid = VERIFY_RESULT(GetPgsqlDatabaseOid(ns.id()));
   vector<TableId> source_table_ids;
   vector<TableId> target_table_ids;
```
Then simply create a 2024.2.3 cluster and try to upgrade:
```
fizaaluthra@fi-mbp-4m2c4 yugabyte-db % ./build/latest/bin/yb-admin --master_addresses 127.0.0.1:7100 upgrade_ysql_major_version_catalog
YSQL major catalog upgrade started
Error running upgrade_ysql_major_version_catalog: Runtime error (yb/util/subprocess.cc:564): Failed to run pg_upgrade: pg_upgrade failed. Check previous errors for more details.: Subprocess '/Users/fizaaluthra/code/yugabyte-db/build/latest/postgres/bin/pg_upgrade' terminated with non-zero exit status 256
```
Here because of our test code the upgrade will fail with the CREATE DATABASE timed out error:
```
command: "/Users/fizaaluthra/code/yugabyte-db/build/debug-clang-dynamic-arm64-ninja/postgres/bin/pg_restore" --host /tmp/.yb.127.0.0.1:5434 --port 5434 --username yugabyte --clean --create --exit-on-error --verbose --dbname template1 "/Users/fizaaluthra/yugabyte-data/node-1/disk-1/pg_upgrade_data/pg_upgrade_output.d/20250930T182956.897/dump/pg_upgrade_dump_13263.custom" >> "/Users/fizaaluthra/yugabyte-data/node-1/disk-1/pg_upgrade_data/pg_upgrade_output.d/20250930T182956.897/log/pg_upgrade_dump_13263.log" 2>&1
pg_restore: connecting to database for restore
pg_restore: dropping DATABASE PROPERTIES yugabyte
pg_restore: dropping DATABASE yugabyte
pg_restore: creating DATABASE "yugabyte"
pg_restore: while PROCESSING TOC:
pg_restore: from TOC entry 2945; 1262 13263 DATABASE yugabyte postgres
pg_restore: error: could not execute query: ERROR:  Timed out waiting for Create Database
Command was: CREATE DATABASE "yugabyte" WITH TEMPLATE = template0 OID = 13263 ENCODING = 'UTF8' LOCALE_PROVIDER = libc LC_COLLATE = 'C' LC_CTYPE = 'en_US.UTF-8';
```
Then rollback:
```
fizaaluthra@fi-mbp-4m2c4 yugabyte-db % ./build/latest/bin/yb-admin --master_addresses  127.0.0.1:7100 rollback_ysql_major_version_catalog                            
YSQL major catalog rollback started
YSQL major catalog rollback completed successfully
```
and then try to upgrade again:
```
fizaaluthra@fi-mbp-4m2c4 yugabyte-db % ./build/latest/bin/yb-admin --master_addresses 127.0.0.1:7100 upgrade_ysql_major_version_catalog 
YSQL major catalog upgrade started
Error running upgrade_ysql_major_version_catalog: Not found (yb/master/catalog_manager.cc:8495): Namespace yugabyte of type 3 not found
```
Root cause:
The buggy code is in `ProcessPendingNamespace` , which does the following cleanup on exit when something in the function fails:
```
  auto cleanup = ScopeExit([this, &status, &ns_write_lock, &ns, &metadata] {
    if (status.ok()) return;
    TRACE("Handling failed keyspace creation");
    // Do not set on-disk state here. The loader treats the PREPARING state as FAILED.
    if (ysql_manager_->IsMajorUpgradeInProgress()) {
      metadata.set_ysql_next_major_version_state(SysNamespaceEntryPB::NEXT_VER_FAILED);
    } else {
      metadata.set_state(SysNamespaceEntryPB::FAILED);
    }
    ns_write_lock.Commit();
    LOG(WARNING) << status.ToString();
    LockGuard lock(mutex_);
    // Remove entry from the by-name map. For YSQL postgres clients cannot issue a DROP
    // DATABASE command at this point because postgres will not commit the metadata for this
    // database to its catalogs. So allow users to create a database with the same name.
    namespace_names_mapper_[ns.database_type()].erase(ns.name());
  });
```
So then when the next upgrade tries to fetch the DB oid for yugabyte it doesn't find it in the namespace map.

